.TH BLIT-UPDATE-HELPER 8 "2026-11-23" "Blit @VERSION@" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
blit-update-helper \- installs Blit packages uploaded through the API
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/lib/blit/bin/blit-update-helper
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B blit-update-helper
is the privileged half of Blit's live update.
A client uploads
.B blit
and
.B blit-compositor
of one version with
.BR "PUT /v1/control/update" ,
the update token, the API token when the server has one (from 0.3.133),
and the release's signature; the server stores each in
.I /var/lib/blit/updates/
and asks the helper to install them.
The server never installs packages itself, so it can run without
root (see
.IR /usr/share/doc/blit/examples/blit-unprivileged.conf ).
.PP
The helper runs as
.BR blit-update-helper.service ,
as root with group blit.
It listens on
.IR /run/blit/update.sock ,
mode 0660, so only the server's group can reach it.
For each request it:
.IP 1. 4
refuses any path that is not a
.I blit-update-*
file directly in
.IR /var/lib/blit/updates/ ;
.IP 2. 4
copies each one, opened once and never through a link, into
.IR /var/lib/blit-update-helper/ ,
which only it can enter; every check below and the install use the copy;
.IP 3. 4
checks each package's SHA-256 against the one the server sent;
.IP 4. 4
checks that the packages are
.B blit
and, optionally,
.BR blit-compositor ,
at one version;
.IP 5. 4
verifies the release signature: the statement
.RS 4
.EX
blit-release-signature 1
blit \fIversion\fP \fIsha256\fP
blit-compositor \fIversion\fP \fIsha256\fP
.EE
.RE
.IP "" 4
rebuilt from what the update carries (each copy's
.B Version
field and SHA-256; the second line only when it carries
.BR blit-compositor ),
must verify, as Ed25519 (RFC 8032), under one of the public keys in
.IR /usr/lib/blit/release-keys/*.pub .
An unsigned update, one signed by any other key, and a signature made for
other packages or another version are refused;
.IP 6. 4
refuses a
.B blit
older than 0.3.133, the first release whose helper verifies signatures,
even when it is signed: such a rollback is root's own
.BR dpkg (1);
.IP 7. 4
refuses an update without
.B blit-compositor
when the host has it installed, because
.B blit-compositor
depends on
.B blit
of exactly its own version; if the host does not have it, it is not added;
.IP 8. 4
installs them with one
.BR dpkg (1)
.B \-\-install \-\-abort\-after=1
\(em
.B blit
first, or on a rollback
.B blit-compositor
first, since
.B blit
breaks every newer compositor \(em stopped after 600 seconds;
.IP 9. 4
removes the staged files and its copies, whether it installed them or refused;
.IP 10. 4
after an install, reloads systemd and restarts
.BR blit.service .
.PP
It replies
.B OK
or
.B ERROR
with the reason: the end of the failing command's output, which carries
dpkg's error. The server returns it to the client.
.PP
It takes no arguments and reads no environment.
.SH PROTOCOL
One line per connection, within 3 seconds:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
UPDATE \fIpath\fP \fIsha256\fP [\fIpath\fP \fIsha256\fP] [SIGNATURE \fIhex\fP]
.EE
.RE
.PP
.I hex
is the release signature, 128 lowercase hex digits, as the client sent it
in
.BR X-Blit-Signature .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
A package was installed; systemd starts the helper again.
.TP
.B 1
The socket could not be created.
.TP
.B 2
Arguments were given.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/blit/update.sock
The socket.
.TP
.I /var/lib/blit/updates/
Uploaded packages, until the helper has answered.
.TP
.I /var/lib/blit-update-helper/
The helper's copies of them, mode 0700, until it has answered.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/blit/release-keys/
The public halves of Blit's release keys, one
.I *.pub
file each, installed by the package. A release adds the next key before
it is used; a key whose file is gone no longer verifies anything.
.TP
.I /etc/blit/update.token
The token the server requires for an update; see
.BR blit.env (5).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR blit (8),
.BR blit.env (5),
.BR dpkg (1)
